==Battleground==
*1 [[Puffsley's Comet]] spawns as the boss after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
*3 [[Corporal Weyland]]s spawn after 50 seconds<sup>1,500f</sup>, delay 40~50 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,500f</sup>.
*1 [[Project A]] spawns after 80 seconds<sup>2,400f</sup>.
*4 [[Star Peng]]s spawn after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>, delay 16.67~20 seconds<sup>500f~600f</sup>.
*4 [[Star Peng]]s spawn after 100 seconds<sup>3,000f</sup>, delay 13.33~16.67 seconds<sup>400f~500f</sup>.
*4 [[Star Peng]]s spawn after 160 seconds<sup>4,800f</sup>, delay 10~13.33 seconds<sup>300f~400f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Star Peng]]s spawn after 206.67 seconds<sup>6,200f</sup>, delay 40~50 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,500f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Even though Puffer Planet is unlocked after clearing [[Cats of the Cosmos]] Chapter 2, don't attempt it immediately, as you will end up facing Star Pengs with up to 15,000% stats depending on your [[Anti-Starred Alien Treasures]]. It's theoretically beatable without all Treasures, but it is not worth the trouble compared to the amount of effort you will have to put in.

The boss of this Advent stage is Puffsey's Comet, an Alien rusher with a low 200 standing range but a huge Omni-Strike to 500 range, alongside high damage and speed. Puffsley also has 400 Knockbacks, meaning even a low damage attack can force a Puffsley rebound and send him rolling straight into your units. Puffsley's main weakness as a boss is his below average health, so using units that naturally have high damage per hit like Can Can, you can minimize the amount of times Puffsley rebounds.

To counter this, this stage spams Star Pengs, with the stage having 12 that appear pretty closely to one another alongside infinite Star Pengs later in the stage. Star Pengs already don't drop too much cash, and without peons like Shibalien or Doge Dark, you'll find yourself very hard pressed for cash, especially when Puffsley wipes out a bunch of your units in one hit. The stage also has three Corporal Weylands and a Project A, which have the range and damage to get damage knockbacks on some of your more fragile units. Making your second priority in this stage killing these enemies is good not only to relieve some pressure, but also to gain money. 

The main strategy to beat this stage is to simply endure the stage out, by quickly killing each Star Peng before they take up too much of your time. Try to be on the offensive throughout the fight, since being defensive will result in Star Pengs stacking up and obliterating anything you send out. While you risk severe cash droughts by going all out, Star Pengs do drop a decent amount of money, so try to be aggressive. 

===Key Units===
*[[Rover Cat (Rare Cat)|Catellite]]: A boosted Catellite will be your best friend, being Immune to Warp and having high stats against Aliens. Make sure it's above level 36 so that it can tank a Puffsley hit.
*[[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]]: Can Can is vital to this stage, having extremely high stats as well as being able to get Money Up kills off Star Peng. You don't need Can Can's Target Alien Talent, but it helps considerably against Puffsley and sole Pengs.
*[[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]]: Cyberpunk is vital to have in this stage thanks to his high range and powerful Slow against Puffsley or hordes of Star Pengs. While Cyberpunk only has one damage knockback and has a long cooldown, while Cyberpunk is up you can have more breathing room for a longer portion of the battle. You need Cyberpunk’s Slow Up Talent to make him worth deploying, as all sending a non-talented Cyber does is make Puffsley attack two seconds earlier than he normally does. 
*[[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]]: Seafarer has pretty decent generalist stats, but more importantly has a high chance to Freeze Aliens as well as a guaranteed Survive, making him very cost effective for Star Peng swarms. Getting Seafarer's Freeze Up Talent increases his chance to Freeze by 20%, making him even more reliable.
===Useful Units===
*[[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]: Due to Puffer Planet's severe cash drought, you will rarely have the opportunity to send Bahamut out against a Weyland / the Project A. You should try to use him mainly for nuking two or three Star Pengs at once, although Bahamut will die very easily if unprotected. 
*[[Wheel Cat (Rare Cat)|Chill Cat]]: Chill has extremely high DPS against Aliens, but suffers from being a huge cash drain regardless of whether or not you own Chill's Cost Down Talent. If you're going to use Chill, try to boost him to 40 so that he can actually deal some damage. A level 42 Chill is able to tank a Star Peng hit, though this is a decent commitment into an otherwise mediocre unit. 
*[[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Slime Cat]]: Slime needs a meatshield to connect onto Star Peng, but its Waves reach far and do huge damage. Having Slime's True Form makes it even more effective, although the Wave level increase can hit Puffsley and cause a damage knockback.
*[[Miter Saw Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Neo Saw Cat]]: Neo Saw has extremely high stats against Aliens, both offensively and defensively. Alongside its Warp Immunity, Saw is able to shred through a good portion of the stage. 
*[[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]]: Bullet Train has high damage and Money Up, but recharges somewhat slowly. If you're not sure what to put in an empty slot, Bullet Train is a fine option.
===Niche Units===
*[[Cossack Cat (Rare Cat)|Royal Guard Cat]]: At level 50 with a Defense Up (Sm) combo, Royal Guard can survive a Puffsley hit, which makes him incredibly powerful alongside Research Combos. While he can beat the entire stage with just a bunch of Research Combos, using him in a normal lineup is not recommended due to him being a massive cash drain for most lineups. Especially considering the lack of reliable cash supplies here, it is best to use Guard only if you are seeking to spam solely him to beat this stage.
*[[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Stone Cat]]: Rock is fairly powerful in this stage as an essentially immortal meatshield that can stall hordes of Star Pengs, but Rock is fairly ineffective without Research combos to decrease its cooldown. In addition, try not to send out Rock liberally, as Stone has enough damage to knockback Puffsley and cause him to start rolling into your units. 

===Recommended Ubers===
*Since this is a mono-Alien stage, anti-Alien Ubers will obviously work here. You’ll want to use anti-Alien Ubers with high stats either offensively or defensively against Aliens, as CC options without any defensive value will just be wastes of cash. Examples include [[Bora (Uber Rare Cat)|Bazibastra]], [[Voli (Uber Rare Cat)|Gigavolta]], [[Gravi (Uber Rare Cat)|Gravolodon]], [[Lumina (Legend Rare Cat)|Luminalia]], [[Radiant Aphrodite (Uber Rare Cat)|Megaphrodite]], [[Warlock and Pierre (Uber Rare Cat)|Mad Doctor Klay]], [[Ganglion (Uber Rare Cat)|Ganglion the Unleashed]], [[Sharpshooter Saki (Uber Rare Cat)|Sharpshooter Saki]], [[Doktor Heaven (Legend Rare Cat)|Professor Abyss]], [[Celestial Child Luna (Uber Rare Cat)|Salvation’s Daughter Lunacia]], [[Lone Moon Lunos (Uber Rare Cat)|Lunos the Eclipsed]], or [[Daybreaker Izanagi (Legend Rare Cat)|Dawnbringer Izanagi]].
*Melee Ubers can also work here, though you’ll need to pay attention to your cash. Examples include [[Lesser Demon Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Greater Balrog Cat]] or [[Baby Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Cats in the Cradle]]. While [[Tecoluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Lufalan Pasalan]] isn’t a melee Uber, he also works here as a unit with high range and single-target damage.

